# Check every text file out with LF on every platform. Without this, git on
# Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true and rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout —
# which is invisible to a Linux-only CI but breaks any test that compares a
# generated string against a file on disk. TestSitesMdInSync did exactly that:
# it regenerates docs/sites.md (LF) and byte-compares, so on the windows-latest
# runner it saw a CRLF file, declared the docs out of sync, and rewrote them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures are byte-exact captures of what a site actually served, and the
# parsers are graded against them. japanhdv's listing.html and detail.html
# genuinely contain CRLF because the site sends it, so line-ending conversion
# in either direction changes what the test is testing. -text takes these out
# of the rule above entirely: git stores and restores them verbatim.
**/testdata/** -text
